WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:08.380
I'm going to start today with something very
pithy and simple that I know is going to get

00:00:08.380 --> 00:00:14.349
some of my audience upset with me, and that's
OK, because we can disagree, I think, which

00:00:14.349 --> 00:00:21.999
is that Barack Obama, former president, was
right to say that the defund the police slogan

00:00:21.999 --> 00:00:26.649
is not a good slogan and that it needs to
be completely renamed.

00:00:26.649 --> 00:00:32.169
And I'm actually reminded of the Ronald Reagan
quote, If you are explaining you are losing.

00:00:32.169 --> 00:00:36.019
Ronald Reagan was correct and Republicans
seem to get this.

00:00:36.019 --> 00:00:37.880
This is one of the biggest failures of the
left.

00:00:37.880 --> 00:00:44.710
If you look at at the work of people like
Thomas Frank and and George Lakoff in particular,

00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:50.320
about naming and framing and slogans, the
left is absolutely terrible at this.

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:55.760
And when you have to explain, well, when I
said defund, I meant this other thing you're

00:00:55.760 --> 00:00:57.129
already losing.

00:00:57.129 --> 00:00:59.859
So let's kind of go through it in layers.

00:00:59.859 --> 00:01:06.090
Actually, defunding and eliminating the police
as a big picture plan doesn't make any sense.

00:01:06.090 --> 00:01:07.930
We've talked about this before.

00:01:07.930 --> 00:01:09.430
It's not reasonable, it's not practical.

00:01:09.430 --> 00:01:14.670
It's not going to happen in any framework
that we can imagine.

00:01:14.670 --> 00:01:18.590
Even places that have done it haven't really
done it.

00:01:18.590 --> 00:01:23.330
Sometimes they've just separated up police
departments into different subgroups or units

00:01:23.330 --> 00:01:24.950
or whatever the case may be.

00:01:24.950 --> 00:01:29.290
Now, some people are saying defund the police,
but they mean something else.

00:01:29.290 --> 00:01:37.729
They mean, you know, will reform mostly in
some places, will have fewer police in others

00:01:37.729 --> 00:01:42.049
will demilitarize and will change how prosecution
is done.

00:01:42.049 --> 00:01:47.210
Well, now you're explaining away a slogan
that doesn't really represent what you mean.

00:01:47.210 --> 00:01:50.000
So why are you using the slogan anyway?

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:53.560
And I've been talking about this since day
one of this slogan.

00:01:53.560 --> 00:01:59.409
During the George Floyd protests, I put out
like a ten or twelve point plan for how I

00:01:59.409 --> 00:02:01.549
would reform the police.

00:02:01.549 --> 00:02:08.940
And many in my audience agreed with demilitarization
training as social workers, extending police

00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:14.550
training periods, stopping what I call low
effort policing.

00:02:14.550 --> 00:02:17.210
It's a very long list which you can go back
to.

00:02:17.210 --> 00:02:21.260
And there were some in my audience who furiously
did not agree with me.

00:02:21.260 --> 00:02:26.020
And I presume that those same folks aren't
going to like what Barack Obama said.

00:02:26.020 --> 00:02:27.730
So what did Barack Obama say?

00:02:27.730 --> 00:02:28.770
Let's take a look at that.

00:02:28.770 --> 00:02:33.900
If you believe as as I do, that we should
be able to reform the criminal justice system

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:38.300
so that it's not biased and treats everybody
fairly.

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:42.310
I guess you can use a snappy slogan like defund
the police.

00:02:42.310 --> 00:02:46.980
But, you know, you've lost a big audience
the minute you say it, which makes it a lot

00:02:46.980 --> 00:02:49.950
less likely that you're actually going to
get the changes you want done.

00:02:49.950 --> 00:02:54.970
But if you instead say, let's reform the police
department so that everybody's being treated

00:02:54.970 --> 00:02:58.830
fairly, you know, divert young people from
getting into crime.

00:02:58.830 --> 00:03:04.140
And if there's a homeless guy, maybe we send
a mental health worker there instead of an

00:03:04.140 --> 00:03:07.380
armed unit that could end up resulting in
a tragedy.

00:03:07.380 --> 00:03:12.060
Suddenly a whole bunch of folks who might
not otherwise listen to you are listening

00:03:12.060 --> 00:03:13.060
to you.

00:03:13.060 --> 00:03:17.270
So the key is deciding, do you want to actually
get something done or do you want to feel

00:03:17.270 --> 00:03:19.830
good among the people you already agree with?

00:03:19.830 --> 00:03:24.340
And if you want to get something done in a
democracy, in a country as big and diverse

00:03:24.340 --> 00:03:29.710
as ours, then you've got to be able to meet
people where they are and play a game of addition

00:03:29.710 --> 00:03:31.170
and not subtraction.

00:03:31.170 --> 00:03:32.980
This is simply pragmatism.

00:03:32.980 --> 00:03:37.270
And Barack Obama actually lists many of the
exact same reforms that I suggested in my

00:03:37.270 --> 00:03:38.780
list some months ago.

00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:42.710
Barack Obama is making the exact same case
that I made about actually getting things

00:03:42.710 --> 00:03:43.710
done.

00:03:43.710 --> 00:03:44.710
That's what I care about.

00:03:44.710 --> 00:03:45.710
I want to get things done.

00:03:45.710 --> 00:03:47.810
Think about it in those terms.

00:03:47.810 --> 00:03:52.730
There are millions of people in the United
States who believe the police should be reformed.

00:03:52.730 --> 00:03:56.300
And you even have allies on areas of the right
on that idea.

00:03:56.300 --> 00:04:01.790
You have some on the libertarian right who
want to reform the drug policing piece of

00:04:01.790 --> 00:04:03.180
police departments.

00:04:03.180 --> 00:04:09.050
You have some on the religious right that
want community programs rather than prison

00:04:09.050 --> 00:04:10.380
for certain crimes.

00:04:10.380 --> 00:04:16.120
You have people like me on the left who want
to end the war on drugs and and police militarization

00:04:16.120 --> 00:04:21.870
and solve the problem of it being so difficult
to hold bad actors accountable due to a system

00:04:21.870 --> 00:04:27.319
that favors police when they're charged with
crimes and prevents this global national bad

00:04:27.319 --> 00:04:28.319
actors database.

00:04:28.319 --> 00:04:29.569
You know, all these different things.

00:04:29.569 --> 00:04:33.460
You have all these different people who could
conceivably work together on this.

00:04:33.460 --> 00:04:37.420
And then you have a tiny portion of people
who actually just want police flatly defunded

00:04:37.420 --> 00:04:39.560
and eliminated in some cases.

00:04:39.560 --> 00:04:46.889
So if what you mean by defund is the things
I mentioned and the things that Barack Obama

00:04:46.889 --> 00:04:53.069
mentioned, then you simply lose potential
allies when the slogan is defund the police

00:04:53.069 --> 00:04:54.360
and the police.

00:04:54.360 --> 00:05:01.680
So I just don't have time when things are
so critical to be toying around with slogans

00:05:01.680 --> 00:05:05.250
that are going nowhere anyway, defund the
police.

00:05:05.250 --> 00:05:11.490
Sounds like you're saying we should take funding
away from police who are bad and do away with

00:05:11.490 --> 00:05:13.210
police as an institution.

00:05:13.210 --> 00:05:18.930
Now, some people do think that if you're somebody
who thinks that we just disagree.

00:05:18.930 --> 00:05:24.160
Most people don't think that they think something
closer to my reform plan.

00:05:24.160 --> 00:05:28.439
So by using the slogan, you're immediately
trying to explain what you really mean and

00:05:28.439 --> 00:05:29.759
that means that you're losing.

00:05:29.759 --> 00:05:32.120
Let me give you one further example.

00:05:32.120 --> 00:05:37.960
One of the things we need are police officers
from more diverse backgrounds.

00:05:37.960 --> 00:05:44.560
And I'm not talking, you know, racially or
religiously or economically, even, although

00:05:44.560 --> 00:05:45.560
that would be good.

00:05:45.560 --> 00:05:46.970
I'm talking culturally.

00:05:46.970 --> 00:05:53.409
You find that in many cities, police are disproportionately
from conservative rural areas outside the

00:05:53.409 --> 00:05:54.509
city.

00:05:54.509 --> 00:05:59.889
One thing that will help fix police is more
people who would do the job the way.

00:05:59.889 --> 00:06:04.169
We want them to do the to do the job people
who are from and even live in those cities

00:06:04.169 --> 00:06:08.400
now, typically the cities are more expensive
than the rural areas.

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:13.689
So sometimes police being underpaid and not
being able.

00:06:13.689 --> 00:06:17.249
People in cities can't live in the cities
on a police salary.

00:06:17.249 --> 00:06:22.139
That's why you get people from the rural conservative
areas coming in because they can come in and

00:06:22.139 --> 00:06:23.889
then live in the cheaper areas.

00:06:23.889 --> 00:06:30.490
You might have to increase funding in those
cases for salaries to get more cultural diversity

00:06:30.490 --> 00:06:31.490
in the police department.

00:06:31.490 --> 00:06:34.480
So how does defend the police help achieve
that?

00:06:34.480 --> 00:06:35.480
It doesn't.

00:06:35.480 --> 00:06:41.330
Now, there's a reasonable counterpoint from
people, including Congresswoman Alexandria

00:06:41.330 --> 00:06:46.039
Castillo Cortez, who says you don't start
with the safe ask.

00:06:46.039 --> 00:06:49.099
You start with more and you negotiate back.

00:06:49.099 --> 00:06:54.370
The problem with that is specifically with
a slogan like defund the police.

00:06:54.370 --> 00:06:57.259
Tons of people tune out because it sounds
wacky.

00:06:57.259 --> 00:07:01.610
It's not like, hey, listen, we'd like twenty
two bucks an hour, so we'll ask for it and

00:07:01.610 --> 00:07:05.770
we'll negotiate down to fifteen because everybody
will participate in the negotiation.

00:07:05.770 --> 00:07:07.439
No, it's not.

00:07:07.439 --> 00:07:14.580
We would love Medicare for all, but we would
negotiate to a strong public option to start.

00:07:14.580 --> 00:07:17.400
And then next year we come back with Medicare
for all.

00:07:17.400 --> 00:07:23.279
If you want to get rid of police altogether,
you immediately get a rejection from a lot

00:07:23.279 --> 00:07:28.809
of the people that are in the reform and they
see you as a non serious actor and it stops

00:07:28.809 --> 00:07:29.809
the conversation.

00:07:29.809 --> 00:07:32.540
So, yes, I agree with President Obama.

00:07:32.540 --> 00:07:35.439
I think he's absolutely right here.

00:07:35.439 --> 00:07:40.039
And we're going to damage our own ability
to fix the problems that we've identified

00:07:40.039 --> 00:07:44.379
by using slogans like defund when it's not
what most people mean and it's never going

00:07:44.379 --> 00:07:45.879
to happen anyway.

00:07:45.879 --> 00:07:47.199
Tell me where I'm wrong.

00:07:47.199 --> 00:08:15.779
I'm ready to have a bigger discussion 

00:08:15.779 --> 00:09:02.910
about it.

